question_en:
Implement two functions:
(1) kinetic_energies(pairs): Takes a list of (m[mg/cm], v[cm/s]) pairs as input, and returns the corresponding list of kinetic energy E[MJ/cm] values (cgs: E=0.5e-3·m·v²/1e13);
(2) velocity_from_energy(m, E): Inversely calculates the velocity (cm/s) from m[mg/cm] and E[MJ/cm].

Implement two functions:
(1) troyon_beta_max(params, beta_N=2.8): params is a dict containing I (MA), a (m), and B (T), and returns the Troyon β limit (%);
(2) greenwald_density(params): returns the Greenwald density limit (1e20 m^-3).
